    "body": "A manpages picker inspired by [telescope.nvim](https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim)'s implementation of the same.\r\n\r\nHere it is in action:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a49e5ee-816a-4a1b-aa1f-ae7adb372aa1\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)",
    "closed_at": "2026-01-04T14:21:43Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI don't think it is a good fit for 'mini.pick' itself, which is meant to contain only minimum amount of essential pickers. It *might* be a good idea for 'mini.extra', but I am a bit hesitant to increase its size even more at this point. It *might* happen, but need some time to weigh some pros and cons here.\r\n\r\nCould you please create a [Show&Tell discussion](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/categories/show-and-tell) instead? This is a good example of a custom picker and we'll probably make it more concise. It will also probably be part of the (hopefully future) wiki.",
